  "key_points": {
    "x": 60, "y": 566, "title": "Key points",
    "items": [
      "Put a 100-220 Ω resistor in each signal line, on the HV side (top row, the small boxes near S21 pins 2 and 3).",
      "Only the two TXI / TXO (MOSFET) columns carry signal. The RXI / RXO divider columns stay empty.",
      "Top row = HV side (5 V, faces aircon); bottom row = LV side (3.3 V, faces XIAO). Both GND pads are in column 4.",
      "Firmware: invert false, UART on GPIO16 / 17 for this hand-wire build. S21 pin 1 (5 V ref) stays unused.",
      "Both TX columns are bidirectional MOSFET lines, so there is no channel-direction trap as long as signals stay off the RX pads.",
      "The XIAO 5 V power pad is silk-labeled **VBUS** on current units (same pad, USB 5 V)."
    ]
  }
